type: comparison
title: Database Options

- Type
  - PostgreSQL: Relational, ACID-compliant
  - MongoDB: Flexible document store
  - Redis: In-memory key-value cache
- Horizontal scaling strategy
  - PostgreSQL: Read replicas and partitioning
  - MongoDB: Built-in sharding across nodes
  - Redis: Cluster mode with hash slots
- Best fit use case
  - PostgreSQL: Complex queries and joins
  - MongoDB: Rapidly evolving schema
  - Redis: Low-latency caching and queues
